{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1096610-resilience-question","id":1096610,"title":"Resilience question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-24T22:19:48-07:00","id":1096610,"title":"Resilience question","content":"As written, Resilience down grades Aggravated damage to Lethal,but not Lethal to bashing. Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T23:26:05-07:00","id":1096629,"title":"","content":"Kindred already downgrade lethal damage into bashing damage. And even without Resilience, Kindred also downgrade aggravated damage from mundane sources to lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T23:27:13-07:00","id":1096630,"title":"","content":"That's just the way the power is designed, honestly. But I imagine that's not a very satisfying answer. There are a couple of reasons you might consider.<br /> \u2022 vampires already downgrade most sources of lethal to bashing naturally, and Resilience is the enhanced form of that ability. Downgrading lethal to bashing would be redundant.<br /> \u2022 If Resilience downgraded aggravated to lethal and lethal to bashing, a vampire with Resilience would basically only ever take bashing damage, unless the damage was in excess of their Resilience dots. Seems a little too strong compared to the other physical Disciplines.<br /> \u2022 Downgrading lethal to bashing is what <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/XPbSdVS4\" target=\"_blank\">.22 Solid</a> is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T23:43:23-07:00","id":1096633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1096610-resilience-question#post1096610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, Resilience down grades Aggravated damage to Lethal,but not Lethal to bashing. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short, it's a non-arbitrary choice to keep Resilience from being too good. Aggravated damage is very rare in 2E, but potentially devastating; lethal damage is less destructive, but more common. Making the negation of lethal damage an active effect forces players to spend resources (Vitae), much like the other physical disciplines, and prevents Resilience from being a must-buy. Indeed, that's why vampires already inherently downgrade most sources of damage. From an in-setting perspective, it's slightly counter intuitive, but it's ultimately for (for lack of a better term) game balance.<br /> <br /> Edit: Charlaquin said it better than I.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T11:58:40-07:00","id":1096813,"title":"","content":"thanks all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T01:22:16-07:00","id":1097035,"title":"","content":"Because that would be <i>too bitchin'</i>.<br /> <br /> More seriously, take another look at .22 Solid and Coil of the Ascendant 4 if you want to upgrade Resilience. If you've got all three, each dot of Resilience gives you the following <i>passively</i> (assume you've got Blush of Life up and you've spent Vitae on .22 Solid):<br /> <br /> 1) +1 Stamina.<br /> 2) Downgrade a level of non-sunlight Aggravated to Lethal.<br /> 3) Downgrade a level of Lethal damage to Bashing.<br /> 4) Downgrade a level of damage from fire to Bashing.<br /> <br /> In other words, spending one Vitae per Scene drops the first [Resilience] points of damage from <i>almost </i><i>any</i> attack to Bashing. By the time you've hit Resilience 3, you can drop one Vitae to prevent the first four points of non-bane damage you take this turn. Then the next 3 levels of damage are Bashing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}